//! Raw declarations for the C ABI. **The only module containing `extern`
//! blocks.**
//!
//! Nothing here is public outside the crate: every item is `pub(crate)`, so the
//! raw structures cannot leak into a caller's types. If a downstream crate could
//! name `supra_ansi_token`, the confinement of `unsafe` to this crate would be
//! nominal rather than real - the caller would end up writing its own unsafe code
//! to use it.
//!
//! Declarations are hand-written rather than generated by bindgen. The ABI is
//! small, stable, and authored in this repository, so a code generator would add
//! a build dependency and a moving part for no benefit. The cost of hand-writing
//! is drift, and that cost is paid down by the compile-time layout assertions
//! below plus the matching `static_assert`s in `abi_check.cpp`.

#![allow(non_camel_case_types)]

use core::ffi::{c_char, c_int, c_void};

/// Layout constants shared with build.rs.
///
/// `abi_sizes.rs` is `include!`d by both this module and build.rs, and build.rs
/// needs the items at its own top level - so they are declared `pub` in the file
/// itself. Inside a private module that reads as unreachable-pub, hence the
/// targeted allow: the visibility is a requirement of the sharing mechanism, not
/// an intent to export.
#[allow(unreachable_pub)]
mod abi {
    include!("../abi_sizes.rs");
}

pub(crate) use abi::*;

